236 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 122 0 R
/E (The Arduino Mega 2560 is a programmable microcontroller board based on the ATmega2560 and is well suited for projects that require a large number of inputs and outputs, such as robotics applications. It consists of a physical electronic board that integrates a microcontroller and can be programmed using the Arduino IDE on a computer. Programs are written in the Arduino programming language, which is based on C/C++, and are uploaded to the board through a USB connection without the need for additional hardware. Compared to smaller boards, the Arduino Mega 2560 provides extended hardware resources. It offers a higher number of digital and analog pins, allowing the connection of multiple sensors and actuators at the same time. This makes it particularly useful in robotic projects where several sensors, motor drivers, and control modules must operate simultaneously. The Arduino Mega 2560 runs at a clock frequency of 16 MHz and includes sufficient memory to handle complex control logic. Its multiple hardware serial communication ports allow reliable communication with external modules such as Bluetooth, ultrasonic sensors, or other control units, without interfering with USB communication used for programming and debugging. Overall, the Arduino Mega 2560 provides a stable and flexible platform for implementing real-time control and decision-making in robotic systems. Its simplicity of programming, combined with powerful hardware capabilities, makes it an appropriate choice for a sumo robot project that requires fast response, multiple sensor inputs, and precise motor control)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
