<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 126 0 R
/E (The L298N is a dual H-bridge motor driver used to control the speed and direction of DC motors. It allows an Arduino to control two DC motors independently by using simple digital and PWM signals. Since the Arduino cannot supply enough current or voltage to drive motors directly, the L298N is used as an interface that provides the required power to the motors. This makes the L298N suitable for robotics applications such as sumo robots, where precise motor control and high torque are required.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
