/T (The TCRT5000 can be directly connected to the Arduino Mega 2560 via its analog input, typically: VCC to 5 V, GND to GND, and AO to A0 \(or another analog input\). The Arduino uses its Analog-to-Digital Converter \(ADC\) to convert the analog voltage into a digital value. The value read by the Arduino is proportional to the surface's infrared reflection, enabling precise line detection, progressive distinction between black and white, and better robot movement control through fine trajectory correction.)
/E (The TCRT5000 can be directly connected to the Arduino Mega 2560 via its analog input, typically: VCC to 5 V, GND to GND, and AO to A0 \(or another analog input\). The Arduino uses its Analog-to-Digital Converter \(ADC\) to convert the analog voltage into a digital value. The value read by the Arduino is proportional to the surface's infrared reflection, enabling precise line detection, progressive distinction between black and white, and better robot movement control through fine trajectory correction.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
